Astralschrot

Ingredients: POWER METAL + NEUROFUNK + ETHEREAL, DREAMY & AIRY + Baritone Saxophone
Creative Catalyst: Musical instruments are forged from iron meteorites and geared with centuries-old cathedral clockwork.

Imagine the thunderous, triumphant gallop of double-kick drums colliding with the violent, tearing sub-bass of neurofunk, then suddenly dissolving into weightless, floating clouds of celestial reverb. Astralschrot sounds like an impossible cathedral in deep space. A heavy baritone saxophone—re-engineered with brass gears and lined with ground chondrite dust—plays roaring, jagged basslines that morph instantly into soaring, operatic melodies. Piercing power metal guitars deliver heroic, twin-lead harmonies, but their distortion tail is stretched into infinite, shimmering fog by analog clockwork delay units, creating a music that is simultaneously hyper-aggressive, mind-bendingly technical, and heartbreakingly serene.

Genre DNA
* Tempo & Pulse: 172–178 BPM. A hybrid rhythm engine that switches seamlessly between the relentless 16th-note double-bass gallop of power metal and the fractured, re-sampled snare rolls and squelching neurofunk neuro-tech breaks.
* Harmonic Palette: Epic Lydian and Mixolydian modes laced with eerie, microtonal inflections caused by the magnetic drift of the meteoric metal. Bright, triumphant major-seventh chords suddenly collapse into harsh, distorted minor intervals.
* Production Signatures: 
  1. Chondrite Resonances: Granular delays fed through mechanical, gear-driven springs that physically tick and whir in rhythm with the master clock.
  2. Sub-Mechanical Splitting: The baritone saxophone low-end is split into a heavily distorted reese-bass sub-track and a crystalline, chorused upper-harmonic mist.
  3. Vacuum-Gated Reverb: Reverb tails that bloom to oceanic size before being violently chopped off by sidechained neurofunk noise gates linked to the kick drum.
* Dynamics: Extreme, heart-stopping contrast. Tracks build from ultra-spacious, drifting ambient silk into blinding explosions of speed, brass roar, and heavy metal euphoria within a single beat.

Scene & Origin Lore
Astralschrot emerged in the subterranean clocktowers beneath Prague, where renegade metal sculptors and breakbeat producers breached the vault of a 14th-century horologist. Finding a cache of nickel-iron meteors preserved in mineral oil, they melted the space-metal down to cast sax-valves, guitar pickups, and motorized mechanical rhythm wheels. The resulting subculture, known as Die Zahnräder ("The Cog-Bearers"), gathers in damp, cavernous stone basilicas for zero-gravity raves. Attendees wear heavy, oil-stained iron pauldrons over translucent gossamer silks and silver face-veil filter masks. The ritual begins at midnight when the central clockwork automaton strikes thirteen, dropping the room from floating, angelic vocal atmospheres into a floor-shattering 175 BPM barrage of cosmic brass and metallic speed.

Central Instruments
* Meteoric Baritone Saxophone: An antique baritone horn fitted with meteoric iron keys and mechanical clockwork valves, delivering raspy sub-bass rasps and glass-shattering solos.
* Gear-Driven Twin Electric Guitars: Flying-V style guitars strung with meteoric wire, running through analog mechanical delay towers.
* Neuro-Chondrite Synthesizer: A custom analog synth whose filters are controlled by physical pendulum gears and magnetic meteoric dust.
* Soprano Operatic Choir: Heavily processed, airy vocal passages layered into dreamy, shimmering clouds.

